#: includes/class-admin.php:513
msgid "Emergency: switch everything off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:514
msgid "If the site or the admin area stops working, use any one of these:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:516
msgid "Add <code>define( 'MG_STEALTH_DISABLE', true );</code> to wp-config.php and open any page of the site: every rule stops, the .htaccess block is removed, wp-login.php works again. Delete the line to switch the plugin on again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:517
msgid "Rename the folder <code>wp-content/plugins/mg-stealth</code> (FTP, file manager). The .htaccess rules check that the plugin file exists, so they stop at once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:518
msgid "WP-CLI: <code>wp mg-stealth remove-rules</code>, <code>wp mg-stealth login-url</code>, <code>wp plugin deactivate mg-stealth</code>."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: path of the .htaccess file
#: includes/class-admin.php:520
#, php-format
msgid "Delete the lines from <code># BEGIN MG Stealth</code> to <code># END MG Stealth</code> in <code>%s</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:522
msgid "Deactivation and removal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:523
msgid "Deactivating removes the .htaccess block and WordPress' rewrite rules are rebuilt: the site is back to its defaults (wp-login.php, /wp-json/, /wp-content/ …). The settings stay for a later activation; deleting the plugin removes them too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:524
msgid "What cannot be hidden"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:526
msgid "Block class names (wp-block-…, wp-container-…) and the CSS custom properties of block themes (--wp--preset--…): styles depend on them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:527
msgid "The header comment of the theme's style.css when the theme loads that file, and @wordpress/… names in the import map of blocks that use the Interactivity API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:528
msgid "Cookies after signing in (wordpress_logged_in_…), and the login page itself at its private address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:529
msgid "Behaviour that a careful tool can still recognise (for example /page/2/ archives). The plugin makes the usual checks find nothing; it cannot promise that no tool ever can."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:531
msgid "Servers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:532
msgid "Apache and LiteSpeed read the .htaccess block. On nginx the PHP part still works (head and headers, REST API, login, authors, XML-RPC, cron, redirects); the neutral paths and the blocking of static files such as readme.html need server rules or the real move from the Paths tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:533
msgid "Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:534
msgid "The plugin sends no data anywhere and prints no credit link. The self-check only asks this site itself. The GitHub build looks for new versions in the GitHub repository of the plugin; the WordPress.org build does not."
msgstr ""

